{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n- `billing-api` pod logs show repeated `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)` (source: Pod logs `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf`).\n- Memory pressure warnings and rising heap usage are reported concurrently in the application logs (source: Pod logs `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf`).\n- Deployment spec sets `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` to 900 seconds (source: Deployment `demo-apps/billing-api`).\n\n### Leads Ruled Out\n- Application memory leak ruled out because memory growth is a byproduct of retained objects from failing connections (source: Runbook `RB-014`).\n- ALB idle timeout mismatch ruled out because resets originate from backend database connection pool acquisition (source: Deployment `CI-2455`, Runbook `RB-014`).\n\n### Root Cause\nDatabase connection pool idle timeout (900 s) exceeds the upstream proxy idle timeout, causing connection pool exhaustion from peer resets (source: Runbook `RB-014`, Incident `INC-2024-0312`).\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe billing team should lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` in `billing-api` Deployment below the upstream proxy idle timeout (source: Runbook `RB-014`).",
